    "body": "<!-- claude-projects-attribution: {\"github_login\":\"siainbuletin\"} -->\n_Requested by **Sia** · [project thread](https://claude.ai/code/project/chan_01KaQfLZaF43QUMN3kcT7pW2?thread=cmsg_01KaQfLZaF43QUMN3kcT7pW22ZZGo68EvQH83Ucp2ATJwU)_\n\nAdds `sp-org-insert-config-doc-link` (`C-c l c` in Org mode), which inserts at point a `file:` link to a file in the configuration docs, from any note (e.g. in `~/notes`), without touching the vulpea database.\n\n- Picks the file with the same fuzzy search as `sp-find-file`, restricted to `.org` files under `sp-config-docs-directory` (`docs/` next to `init.el`).\n- `file:` link with the path abbreviated to `~/`; the docs have no `:ID:`, and an `id:` link would need them in the database. Description defaults to the file's `#+title` (prefix argument asks for it).\n- `sp-navi`: `sp-find-file` is split into `sp-find-file-options`, `sp-find-file--read` and the new `sp-find-file-pick`; `C-x C-f` behaves as before.\n- Literate docs of `sp-navi`, `sp-org-id-link` and `sp-org-base` updated and checked to match the code.\n\nNot run in Emacs (none in the container).\n\n---\n_Generated by [Claude Code](https://claude.ai/code/session_01WWLNi8uXRpRhW9D9Zpm3ps)_",
